# input file for particle conversion to/from EPOS
# the format of this file is: "corsika-identifier" "epos-id" "can-interact-in-epos" "cross-section-type"
# Some of the higher resonances in Epos are grouped into a single particle, 
# e.g N(1520)0 and N(1535)0 are the same state (internal id: 1223) 
# For these particles there is no unique conversion between Epos and Corsika.
# Since we are only interested in particle production from Epos we map 
# the effective states to the lightest resonance.

# The unknown particle is to handle all particles that are not known to EPOS.
# It is important that epos-id does not overlap with any existing epos particle!
# Be careful
Unknown                  0       0       CannotInteract

# Here is the list of particles known to EPOS
Photon                   10      0       CannotInteract
